  "period_note": "Year-end (31 December 2013) position from NRB Commercial Bank's own audited annual report multi-year key-financial table, taken from the FY2015 report. Basis note: the FY2015-FY2019 summary tables are CONSOLIDATED — the FY2018 report's 67,142.86 for FY2018 is its consolidated balance-sheet total, against 67,061.86 solo, a 0.12% difference — while the FY2020 and later tables are SOLO. The gap is immaterial in size but the basis genuinely changes at FY2020 and should be treated as a break when comparing across it. Off-balance-sheet trap: the FY2022 report's summary table prints FY2018 total assets as 86,598.12, which is that year's balance-sheet total (67,142.86) plus its off-balance-sheet items (19,455.25) — the sum is exact. Its FY2019 and later columns exclude off-balance-sheet items. This dataset never sources FY2018 total assets from that report. The FY2021 report is excluded entirely: its only extractable table is a horizontal analysis in which every value is a percentage of a base year, so it carries no usable figures at all. The FY2013 annual report is not usable as a source (it is absent from the archive, or extracts with no summary table), so this year comes from the FY2015 report. NRB Commercial Bank opened in April 2013, so FY2013 is a part-year. Classified loans and the NPL ratio are recorded as nil: the FY2015 report prints no classified-loan figure for FY2013 or FY2014, and the first reported classified loans appear in FY2015 (0.27%). Calculated line item(s): total_capital, car_pct. total_capital, where derived, is this report's own Tier-I plus Tier-II rather than a later report's total, so the capital stack stays internally consistent. car_pct, where derived, is total capital over risk-weighted assets. classified_loans, where derived, is the reported ratio applied to reported loans and advances. RESTATEMENTS -- 1 figure(s) here differ in other NRBC reports; the contemporaneous value is kept: paid_up_capital: this record uses 4446.06 (AR2015); AR2017 report 4373.85.",
